<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LanguageData>

  <!-- Settings: window category (mod-list entry). "melee weapon" follows Core's ThingCategoryDef
       WeaponsMelee ("armas de corpo a corpo"); the unhyphenated form dominates the corpus 56 to 9. -->
  <!-- EN: Unique Melee Weapons -->
  <UMW_SettingsCategory>Armas de corpo a corpo únicas</UMW_SettingsCategory>

  <!-- Settings: section headers. "Trait abilities" heads the tuning of the abilities some weapon
       traits grant (the word "trait" as in weapon trait, the same word as the Traits header). The
       quest section's header is "{0} quest" with {0} the warband faction's def label, capitalized
       and already localized, so it reads "Warband quest"; phrase it so the injected name needs no
       inflection. -->
  <!-- EN: Weapons -->
  <UMW_SettingsWeapons>Armas</UMW_SettingsWeapons>

  <!-- EN: Traits -->
  <UMW_SettingsTraits>Características</UMW_SettingsTraits>

  <!-- EN: Generation -->
  <UMW_SettingsGeneration>Geração</UMW_SettingsGeneration>

  <!-- EN: Traders -->
  <UMW_SettingsTraders>Comerciantes</UMW_SettingsTraders>

  <!-- EN: Trait abilities -->
  <UMW_SettingsTraitAbilities>Habilidades das características</UMW_SettingsTraitAbilities>

  <!-- EN: {0} quest -->
  <UMW_SettingsQuestSection>Missão: {0}</UMW_SettingsQuestSection>

  <!-- EN: Compatibility -->
  <UMW_SettingsCompat>Compatibilidade</UMW_SettingsCompat>

  <!-- Settings: reusable label suffixes. Each includes a leading space, and every applicable one is
       appended (no precedence between them), so they must read cleanly back to back. -->
  <!-- EN:  (default) -->
  <UMW_DefaultSuffix> (padrão)</UMW_DefaultSuffix>

  <!-- {0} is another piece of content the current value matches, named from its own def label
       (the ancient-mercenaries site part, "Mercenários Anciões"). Its gender is unknowable here, so
       the suffix reaches it through "a" with no article rather than a contracted "ao/à". -->
  <!-- EN:  (same as {0}) -->
  <UMW_SameAsSuffix> (igual a {0})</UMW_SameAsSuffix>

  <!-- Checkbox-row suffixes, at most one per row, each with a leading space. The first is appended
       to a group header (which is the bare name of a mod or DLC) only while that mod or DLC is not
       installed or not enabled, so the greyed header reads "Royalty (3) (not active)". {0} in the second
       is a weapon's def label (lowercase): the row is a trait that cannot be turned off because it is
       the last trait that weapon could roll first, so the box is held on. -->
  <!-- EN:  (not active) -->
  <UMW_NotActiveSuffix> (inativo)</UMW_NotActiveSuffix>

  <!-- EN:  (last trait for {0}) -->
  <UMW_LastTraitSuffix> (última característica para {0})</UMW_LastTraitSuffix>

  <!-- EN:  (requires restart) -->
  <UMW_RequiresRestartSuffix> (requer reinício)</UMW_RequiresRestartSuffix>

  <!-- Settings: grouped rows. In the Weapons and Traits sections, the rows an optional mod or DLC
       adds sit under a header that is just that mod or DLC's name and its row count (coloured, no
       extra text), with a three-state box that switches the whole group. The first string is the
       count, with a leading space, appended to the name in the name's colour so the header reads
       "Royalty (3)"; {0} is how many weapons or traits this mod adds for that mod or DLC in that
       section, shown even while it is not active. The second is the header's tooltip; {0} is the name,
       injected already coloured: do not inflect it. The last sentence describes click-and-drag
       painting over the checkbox rows beneath the header. -->
  <!-- EN:  ({0}) -->
  <UMW_GroupCountSuffix> ({0})</UMW_GroupCountSuffix>
  <!-- EN: Everything from {0} in this section. The box switches the whole group at once; a half-filled box means some of its rows are off. Click and drag across the rows below to switch several at once. -->
  <UMW_IntegrationGroupDesc>Tudo de {0} nesta seção. A caixa alterna o grupo inteiro de uma vez; uma caixa meio preenchida indica que algumas linhas estão desativadas. Clique e arraste pelas linhas abaixo para alternar várias de uma vez.</UMW_IntegrationGroupDesc>
  <!-- EN: Traits original to {0}, of its own design. The box switches the whole group at once; a half-filled box means some of its rows are off. Click and drag across the rows below to switch several at once. -->
  <UMW_OwnTraitsGroupDesc>Características originais de {0}, de design próprio. A caixa alterna o grupo inteiro de uma vez; uma caixa meio preenchida indica que algumas linhas estão desativadas. Clique e arraste pelas linhas abaixo para alternar várias de uma vez.</UMW_OwnTraitsGroupDesc>
  <!-- EN: Melee counterparts of the traits {0} gives its unique ranged weapons. The box switches the whole group at once; a half-filled box means some of its rows are off. Click and drag across the rows below to switch several at once. -->
  <UMW_OdysseyTraitsGroupDesc>Equivalentes corpo a corpo das características que {0} dá às suas armas à distância únicas. A caixa alterna o grupo inteiro de uma vez; uma caixa meio preenchida indica que algumas linhas estão desativadas. Clique e arraste pelas linhas abaixo para alternar várias de uma vez.</UMW_OdysseyTraitsGroupDesc>

  <!-- Fallback display names, used only while the mod is not installed. Proper nouns: kept verbatim. -->
  <!-- EN: Vanilla Factions Expanded - Pirates -->
  <UMW_ModNameVfePirates>Vanilla Factions Expanded - Pirates</UMW_ModNameVfePirates>

  <!-- EN: Vanilla Textures Expanded -->
  <UMW_ModNameVte>Vanilla Textures Expanded</UMW_ModNameVte>

  <!-- Settings: Weapons. One checkbox per weapon. {0} is the weapon's own def label (lowercase), whose
       gender varies (machado único / espada longa única) and which nothing inflects for us, so the
       Portuguese never agrees with {0}: it names the subject as "esta arma" once and keeps every later
       reference on that feminine noun. -->
  <!-- EN: Allow {0} to be generated. Turn off to remove it from every reward and loot pool; the other weapons fill its place. Weapons already in your save are untouched. -->
  <UMW_WeaponEnabledDesc>Permitir a geração desta arma: {0}. Desative para removê-la de todos os grupos de recompensas e de pilhagem; as outras armas ocupam o lugar dela. Armas já existentes no seu jogo salvo não são afetadas.</UMW_WeaponEnabledDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Traits. One checkbox per trait. {0} is the trait's own def label (lowercase). -->
  <!-- EN: Allow {0} to roll on newly made unique weapons. Turn off to keep it out of the roll; other traits fill its place. Weapons that already carry it keep it. -->
  <UMW_TraitEnabledDesc>Permitir que a característica {0} seja sorteada em armas únicas recém-criadas. Desative para tirá-la do sorteio; as outras características ocupam o lugar dela. Armas que já a possuem a mantêm.</UMW_TraitEnabledDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Generation -->
  <!-- {0} is the wood resource's item label (ThingDef WoodLog, "madeira", lowercase). -->
  <!-- EN: Exclude {0} from generated unique weapons -->
  <UMW_ExcludeWoodStuff>Excluir {0} das armas únicas geradas</UMW_ExcludeWoodStuff>

  <!-- {0} is the vanilla longsword's item label (lowercase), named as the example reward. It is an
       injected label, so the Portuguese reaches it through the vanilla material frame "de madeira"
       (Core's ThingMadeOfStuffLabel is "{1} de {0}") and puts no article in front of it: "na forma de
       {0} de madeira" needs no gender agreement. -->
  <!-- EN: Unique weapons roll a random eligible material. With this on, wood is never rolled, so a hard-won reward never lands as a wooden {0}. -->
  <UMW_ExcludeWoodStuffDesc>Armas únicas sorteiam um material válido ao acaso. Com esta opção ativada, a madeira nunca é sorteada, para que uma recompensa duramente conquistada nunca chegue na forma de {0} de madeira.</UMW_ExcludeWoodStuffDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Traders. Both toggles default off. The row label is a shared template: {0} is the
       trader kind's own def label, capitalized ("Comerciantes de guerra", "Comerciantes xamãs" -
       vanilla pt-BR renders these TraderKindDef labels as plural nouns even though the English
       source is singular, so the injected value already carries its own agreement); each
       description's {0} is the same label in lowercase, as vanilla already ships it. -->
  <!-- EN: Unique weapons in {0} stock -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniques>Armas únicas em estoque: {0}</UMW_TraderStocksUniques>

  <!-- EN: About half of {0} visits bring one unique melee weapon of medieval or older make for sale, and the caravan buys unique melee weapons either way. Ultratech traits never roll on its stock: a war party deals in period arms. Disabled weapons never appear. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesWarMerchantDesc>Cerca de metade das visitas de {0} traz uma arma corpo a corpo única de fabricação medieval ou mais antiga à venda, e a caravana compra armas corpo a corpo únicas de qualquer forma. Características ultratecnológicas nunca são sorteadas em seu estoque: uma tropa de guerra negocia com armas de sua própria época. Armas desativadas nunca aparecem.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesWarMerchantDesc>

  <!-- EN: About half of {0} visits bring one unique melee weapon of medieval or older make for sale, and the caravan buys unique melee weapons either way. Ultratech traits may roll on its stock: shamans trade in relics they do not fully understand. Disabled weapons never appear. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShamanDesc>Cerca de metade das visitas de {0} traz uma arma corpo a corpo única de fabricação medieval ou mais antiga à venda, e a caravana compra armas corpo a corpo únicas de qualquer forma. Características ultratecnológicas podem ser sorteadas em seu estoque: xamãs negociam com relíquias que não compreendem totalmente. Armas desativadas nunca aparecem.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShamanDesc>

  <!-- Outlander rows, shown only while some unique weapon is of industrial or later make. The
       settlement row's text is fixed (the trader kind has no def label of its own); the caravan and
       trade ship rows add a qualifier because the two combat suppliers share one vanilla label:
       {0} is that label (plural noun phrase, "Comerciantes de combate"), capitalized in the row
       label and lowercase in the description, so it is quoted inside parentheses rather than
       agreed. "forasteiro" is the vanilla outlander term (OutlanderCivil/Rough faction labels,
       "União Forasteira"); medieval / industrial are vanilla's TechLevel names, identical in pt-BR. -->
  <!-- EN: Unique weapons in Outlander settlement stock -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesOutlanderSettlement>Armas únicas em estoque: assentamento forasteiro</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesOutlanderSettlement>

  <!-- EN: About one in five outlander settlements stocks one unique melee weapon of industrial or later make, and it buys unique melee weapons either way. Disabled weapons never appear. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesOutlanderSettlementDesc>Cerca de um em cada cinco assentamentos forasteiros tem em estoque uma arma corpo a corpo única de fabricação industrial ou mais recente, e compra armas corpo a corpo únicas de qualquer forma. Armas desativadas nunca aparecem.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesOutlanderSettlementDesc>

  <!-- EN: Unique weapons in {0} caravan stock -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesCaravan>Armas únicas em estoque: caravana ({0})</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesCaravan>

  <!-- EN: About one in five {0} caravan visits brings one unique melee weapon of industrial or later make for sale, and the caravan buys unique melee weapons either way. Disabled weapons never appear. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesCaravanDesc>Cerca de uma em cada cinco visitas de caravana ({0}) traz uma arma corpo a corpo única de fabricação industrial ou mais recente à venda, e a caravana compra armas corpo a corpo únicas de qualquer forma. Armas desativadas nunca aparecem.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesCaravanDesc>

  <!-- EN: Unique weapons in {0} trade ship stock -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShip>Armas únicas em estoque: nave comercial ({0})</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShip>

  <!-- EN: About one in five {0} trade ships carries one unique melee weapon of industrial or later make for sale, and the ship buys unique melee weapons either way. Disabled weapons never appear. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShipDesc>Cerca de uma em cada cinco naves comerciais ({0}) traz uma arma corpo a corpo única de fabricação industrial ou mais recente à venda, e a nave compra armas corpo a corpo únicas de qualquer forma. Armas desativadas nunca aparecem.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShipDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Trait abilities. Each ability is a subsection headed by its own icon and name (from
       its def, already localized) followed by the first string, which names in parentheses the
       weapon trait that grants it ("Earthshake (Piledriver)"); it has a leading space and {0} is
       that trait's def label, capitalized and already localized. The ability's description is the
       header's tooltip, so the slider rows beneath name only the property: in the next three, {0}
       is the slider's current value. The unit word is part of the template, so hour- and day-based
       cooldowns are separate keys. The last row tunes a different def from the ability above it
       (the rallied buff), so it keeps the subject: {0} is that hediff's def label, capitalized; {1}
       is the value.
       Portuguese keeps the last row's {0} first, as English does, and follows it with a colon.
       Reaching the label through a preposition would want a contracted article ("a duração do
       ânimo"), and the label's gender is unknowable here while nothing in the language worker fuses
       "de" with an article for us. Naming the subject first sidesteps that entirely. -->
  <!-- EN:  ({0}) -->
  <UMW_TraitAbilitySuffix> ({0})</UMW_TraitAbilitySuffix>
  <!-- EN: Cooldown: {0} hours -->
  <UMW_CooldownHours>Tempo de recarga: {0} horas</UMW_CooldownHours>

  <!-- EN: Cooldown: {0} days -->
  <UMW_CooldownDays>Tempo de recarga: {0} dias</UMW_CooldownDays>

  <!-- EN: Radius: {0} cells -->
  <UMW_RadiusCells>Raio: {0} células</UMW_RadiusCells>

  <!-- EN: {0} duration: {1} hours -->
  <UMW_HediffDurationHours>{0}: duração de {1} horas</UMW_HediffDurationHours>

  <!-- {0} is the Odyssey DLC's name, injected already coloured: do not inflect it. -->
  <!-- EN: Rest time between earthshakes. The default matches the EMP pulser from {0}. 0 removes the cooldown. -->
  <UMW_EarthshakeCooldownDesc>Tempo de descanso entre dois tremores de terra. O valor padrão corresponde ao pulsador PEM de {0}. Com 0, o tempo de recarga é removido.</UMW_EarthshakeCooldownDesc>

  <!-- EN: Reach of the stunning shockwave. Walls do not stop it; gaps with no floor do. It is indiscriminate: a wider radius catches your own colonists too. -->
  <UMW_EarthshakeRadiusDesc>Alcance da onda de choque atordoante. Paredes não a detêm; vãos sem piso, sim. Ela não distingue amigos de inimigos: um raio maior também atinge seus próprios colonos.</UMW_EarthshakeRadiusDesc>

  <!-- EN: Rest time between rallying cries. Measured in days on purpose: the default makes it an heirloom moment, not a standing aura re-applied every fight. -->
  <UMW_RallyingCryCooldownDesc>Tempo de descanso entre dois gritos de guerra. Medido em dias de propósito: com o valor padrão isso vira um momento digno de uma relíquia de família, e não uma aura permanente reaplicada em cada combate.</UMW_RallyingCryCooldownDesc>

  <!-- EN: How far the cry carries. Rallies every non-hostile humanlike in range with line of sight; blocked by walls. Also wakes sleepers. -->
  <UMW_RallyingCryRadiusDesc>Até onde o grito alcança. Encoraja todo humanoide não hostil dentro do alcance que tenha linha de visão; bloqueado por paredes. Também acorda quem está dormindo.</UMW_RallyingCryRadiusDesc>

  <!-- EN: How long the rallied buff lasts, halving pain and stagger time. Sleepers are woken instead, and resent it. -->
  <UMW_RalliedDurationDesc>Quanto tempo o efeito do grito dura, reduzindo à metade a dor e o tempo de cambaleio. Quem está dormindo acorda em vez de recebê-lo, e não gosta nada disso.</UMW_RalliedDurationDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Warband quest. The section is headed by the camp's world-map icon and the
       UMW_SettingsQuestSection header above. The first string is that header's tooltip,
       describing the quest; {0} is the Odyssey DLC's name, injected already coloured: do not
       inflect it. "Ancient mercenaries" is the vanilla quest's name; translate it to match the
       official localization. The second is the slider row's label; {0} is the slider's current
       value. The desc's quest examples (ancient mercenaries, bandit camps, item stashes) are
       vanilla content names too. Taken here from the official localization (Odyssey's
       questSubjectRules, Core's BanditCamp and ItemStash SitePartDefs). -->
  <!-- EN: An opportunity-site quest: a tribal warband holed up in an abandoned settlement, led by a chief who carries a unique melee weapon. Capture or kill the chief to take it. The low-tech counterpart of the ancient mercenaries quest from {0}. -->
  <UMW_WarbandQuestDesc>Uma missão de local de oportunidade: um bando de guerra tribal entrincheirado em um assentamento abandonado, liderado por um chefe que carrega uma arma corpo a corpo única. Capture ou mate o chefe para ficar com ela. A versão de baixa tecnologia da missão dos mercenários antigos presente em {0}.</UMW_WarbandQuestDesc>

  <!-- EN: Commonality: {0} -->
  <UMW_QuestCommonality>Frequência de missão: {0}</UMW_QuestCommonality>

  <!-- EN: How often the warband quest is offered against the other opportunity-site quests (ancient mercenaries, bandit camps, item stashes...). Higher = offered more often. 0 disables it. -->
  <UMW_WarbandQuestWeightDesc>Com que frequência a missão do bando de guerra é oferecida frente às outras missões de locais de oportunidade (mercenários antigos, acampamentos de bandidos, esconderijos de itens...). Mais alto = oferecida mais vezes. Com 0, a missão fica desativada.</UMW_WarbandQuestWeightDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Compatibility. Shown only when Vanilla Textures Expanded is active. The toggle
       defaults on and is read when the game loads, hence the restart sentence. {0} is our unique
       spear's def label (lowercase); {1} is that mod's display name from its About.xml, injected so
       neither is restated here. Deliberately says nothing about performance. -->
  <!-- EN: Match the {0} to {1} -->
  <UMW_MatchVteSpear>Fazer a {0} corresponder a {1}</UMW_MatchVteSpear>

  <!-- EN: {1} draws the vanilla spear diagonally and longer. With this on, the {0} is turned and enlarged to match it in a drafted pawn's hands. Purely cosmetic. Takes effect after a restart. -->
  <UMW_MatchVteSpearDesc>{1} redesenha a lança do jogo base na diagonal e mais comprida. Com esta opção ativada, a {0} é girada e aumentada para corresponder a ela nas mãos de um colono alistado. Puramente estético. Tem efeito depois de reiniciar o jogo.</UMW_MatchVteSpearDesc>

</LanguageData>
